# framehaptix: give the logged-in (seat) user access to the hidraw node(s) of
# the Framework haptic touchpad (PIXA3854), so settings can be applied without
# sudo. Must sort before 73-seat-late.rules for TAG+="uaccess" to take effect.
#
# The touchpad is an ACPI-enumerated I2C-HID device. Its I2C client (a parent of
# the hidraw node) carries a sysfs `name` attribute like "PIXA3854:00", which is
# what ATTRS{name} matches here. Verify on your machine with:
#   udevadm info -a -n /dev/hidrawN | grep -i 'ATTRS{name}'
# and open an issue/PR if your board reports something different.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{name}=="*PIXA3854*", TAG+="uaccess"
